# Fixed defect 132's class, 2026-09-29, a foreign word the parser reads as
# its certain swap, at a line break, the boundary of
# `fixedbugs-132-a-line-a-refused-word-heads-opens-no-break.hero`. Symptom,
# of lane 133's first round: `5 +` left open over `fn main()` cost
# `continuation_outside_brackets` beside `reserved_word` and, once `check
# --apply` had written `function`, `expected_expression`, one mistake under
# two codes; the `)` below it was told only after the swap. Lane 133 made
# the lexer ask what the word's swap writes (`next_line.opening_keyword`),
# and lane Y measured it held on its tree; no case held the shape until this
# one. And its other side: a line such a word heads is the line its swap
# heads, so `fn two() ->` over `i64` is refused as `function two() ->` is,
# and a line a refused word heads opens no break only where the parser reads
# the word as nothing. Each mistake takes the same code before and after
# `--apply` writes the swaps, which the `.applied` pins.

constant A: i64
    #~v expected_expression
    5 +
fn main()  #~ reserved_word
    x = 3 )  #~ expected_end_of_line

#~v reserved_word continuation_outside_brackets
fn two() ->
i64
    return 2
